-- title:
--   O(n log n) multitape multiplication from any recursive step satisfying StepOK
-- statement:
--   Let `st` be a recursive step (an `RM` program) satisfying `StepOK st n₀ lin calls`: on inputs $a,b<2^N$ with $N \ge n_0$ it pushes $a\cdot b$, it costs at most $\mathrm{lin}(N)+\sum_{(c,m)\in \mathrm{calls}(N)} c\,Φ(m)$ when every recursive multiplication of $m$-bit numbers costs at most $Φ(m)$, all recursive sizes $m$ are $<N$, and its procedure calls are the fixed DIF/DIT/bit-length procedures. Let $T'(N) = (N+1)(\mathrm{zsz}(N)+2)$ ($\approx N\log N$). Suppose there are constants $K$ and $D\ge 1$ such that for all $N \ge n_0$
--   - $\mathrm{topCost}(n_0,N)+\mathrm{lin}(N)+2 \le K\,T'(N)$ (the non-recursive work is $O(N\log N)$), and
--   - $D\sum_{(c,m)\in\mathrm{calls}(N)} c\,T'(m) + T'(N) \le D\,T'(N)$ (the recursive calls leave room for the linear term).
--
--   Then integer multiplication is possible on a multitape Turing machine in time $O(n\log n)$: `MulTimeBound (fun n => n * log n)` holds, in the sense of the platform model `Def_IntMul_MultitapeModel`.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The machine is `hvMachine n₀ st`, compiled from a five-procedure item-language program (main routine, the multiplication procedure `mulRM n₀ st` which uses schoolbook multiplication below $n_0$ bits and `st` above, DIF, DIT, bit length). This is the conditional top level of the Harvey–van der Hoeven machine: proving Theorem 1.1 reduces to exhibiting such a step. The machine layer: `IState HS` is a state with $64$ stacks of items (`Item` = integer or mark), an input position and an output; `RM` programs (straight-line register code `RS`, loops `rep`, conditionals, calls of the multiplication procedure through a `MulSpec` $M$ giving its domain and cost) have a functional semantics `p.run s`, a definedness predicate `p.ok M s` and a cost `p.cost M s`; `Spec M p s s' c` abbreviates `p.ok M s ∧ p.run s = s' ∧ p.cost M s ≤ c`. `ints L` / `gints U` push an integer list / a list of pairs as items (head = top); `zsz z` is the bit length of $|z|$. `MulBnd M m Φ` says the multiplication procedure accepts all pairs of integers of bit length $\le m$ at cost $\le Φ$. Register names (`GU`, `CR`, `KB`, `XN`, …) are fixed stack indices.
-- source:
--   D. Harvey, J. van der Hoeven, Integer multiplication in time O(n log n), Ann. of Math. 193 (2021), 563–617 (Theorem 1.1: multitape Turing machine multiplication in O(n log n)). Lemma `NLogN.Top.hv_mulTimeBound` of the Lean development NLogN/HTopFinal.lean (lines 67–80), written for the prove2.me integer-multiplication campaign.

